================================================================================
TEST 38395 — Traffic forwarding over dynamic aggregators (LACP)
================================================================================
Date        : 2026-08-19
Bench       : tb470
DUT         : AT-IE520-28GSX two-member VCStack, virtual-chassis-id 3439,
              VMAC 0000.cd37.0d6f
              member 1 = S/N 264A23066, MAC 84e3.2787.0740, console /dev/u5
              member 2 = S/N 264A23052, MAC 84e3.2787.09c0, console /dev/u4
Software    : IE520-tb470.rel (IE520-tomahawk_ie520-continuous.rel, 2026-08-19)
Companion   : 38385.log is the identical test over STATIC channels. Same rig,
              same traffic, same steps — the pair differ only in LACP vs static.
              See 38393.log for the LAG build and the bootloader netboot finding.

VERDICT: ALL 5 STEPS PASS.
         Traffic forwarded over LACP aggregators that span both stack members,
         continued across a master reboot, and continued when the aggregators
         were cut down to a single leg on opposite members so that every frame
         had to traverse the stack link.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TOPOLOGY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
No Ixia on this bench; tb470 generates and receives with tcpreplay/tcpdump.

  tb470 eth1 ── AR4050 p1.0.1 │ po1 ┬ p1.0.3 ── DUT port1.0.1 (m1) ┐
                                    └ p1.0.4 ── DUT port2.0.9 (m2) ┘ DUT po1
                                                                     vlan 393
  tb470 eth2 ── x230   p1.0.1 │ po1 ┬ p1.0.2 ── DUT port2.0.1 (m2) ┐
                                    └ p1.0.4 ── DUT port1.0.9 (m1) ┘ DUT po2

Single bridged vlan 393 across both aggregators (this is an L2 forwarding test;
the routed vlan 394/395 config from 38396 was reverted first, back to 1 connected
route). Port-to-port mapping was measured by bouncing each neighbour port — see
38393.log.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1 — Check the precondition and set up the DUT topology              PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Stack: member 1 Ready/Backup, member 2 Ready/Active Master, Normal operation,
Stack MAC 0000.cd37.0d6f (Virtual MAC). Stack link port1.0.28 <-> port2.0.27.
All four data ports connected in vlan 393 at a-full/a-1000.

